    "q-182493": {
      "dom_id": "step-q182493",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Simplify the statement $M⇒¬N.$",
      "worked_solution": "The conditional statement $P⇒Q$ is logically equivalent to the disjunction $¬P∨Q:$\n\nSo, in this case, we have the following equivalence:\n\n$$\nM⇒¬N≡¬M∨¬N\n$$\n\nUsing De Morgan's law, we reach\n\n$$\n¬M∨¬N≡¬(M∧N).\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $¬(M∧N).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-182493-a",
