    "q-102734": {
      "dom_id": "step-q102734",
      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "Simplify the statement $¬(¬A∨¬B)⇒¬A.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that\n\n$$\n¬(¬A∨¬B)⇒¬A≡¬(¬(¬A∨¬B))∨¬A.\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negations, we reach\n\n$$\n¬(¬(¬A∨¬B))∨¬A≡(¬A∨¬B)∨¬A.\n$$\n\nUsing the commutative and associative law, we have\n\n$$\n(¬A∨¬B)∨¬A≡(¬A∨¬A)∨¬B.\n$$\n\nFinally, by the idempotent law, we have\n\n$$\n(¬A∨¬A)∨¬B≡¬A∨¬B.\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $¬A∨¬B.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
